  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the officers as 'you and ya partner'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the two police officers in the image, who are explicitly referred to as 'you and ya partner' in the top text. The visual depiction of the officers smiling and looking at each other, along with the textual context, invites the viewer to identify with them as the subjects of the scenario — the two colleagues engaging in playful deception about the donuts. This projection is reinforced by the informal language 'ya' and the shared, conspiratorial body language, which signals familiarity and camaraderie. The user is thus invited to imagine themselves in the officers' shoes, experiencing the humorous moment of pretending there are no donuts left when there are actually two.",
